{
	"version": 1,

	"_comment": "What every combat action LOOKS like (client only; the rules never read this). Each action key maps to a list of layers that play together. Adding or changing an effect is a data change here. KEYS: 'swing/<move id>' (the move's damaging frames begin; falls back to 'swing/<kind>' such as swing/light_1, swing/heavy, swing/run_light, then 'swing/default'), 'windup/<move id or kind>' (the move starts: skills and telegraphed monster moves), 'land/<move id or kind>' (a diving move touches the ground), 'hit' (+ 'hit/heavy', 'hit/crit', 'hit/launch', 'hit/knockback', 'hit/armored' and 'hit/<move id or kind>' when they apply, see hit_rules), 'block', 'guard_break', 'poise_break', 'dodge', 'run_dust', 'land', 'knockdown', 'getup', 'death', 'loot', 'rest', 'status/<effect control or kind>'. LAYERS: type trail (a brush stroke: shape arc/thrust/ring, radius, width, from/to = degrees from the facing for arcs or distances along it for thrusts, rise = [height at start, height at end], tilt = roll of the stroke plane in degrees, yaw = extra turn, sweep = part of the life the head needs to cross the stroke, tail = visible tail length, lanes/lane_gap = parallel copies), sprite (mode glow/star/splat/ring/beam/swirl/ghost/cross, size = [from, to], height = stretch upward, billboard camera/y/ground, spin = degrees per second, spikes), ground (mode ring/crack/stain/glyph, size = [from, to]), burst (one draw call of up to 32 particles: style streak/puff/mote, count, speed, spread = cone half angle in degrees, dir up/down/forward/back/none, lift = degrees above the ground for forward/back, gravity, drag, size, streak), ghosts (afterimages along a moving fighter: count, interval), shake (strength, seconds), punch (degrees of zoom), flash (screen color). COMMON: seconds, delay, color (a palette name, 'weapon' = the attacker's color / the item tier, '#rrggbb', or [r, g, b, a]), ink (0 = pure color, 1 = dark ink), anchor (at = the action's point, feet, chest, hitbox), offset = [forward, up, side], scale = true to grow with the hit's damage (see hit_rules: count and shake grow by the factor, size and speed by its square root), opacity. 'base' = also play all layers of another key first.",

	"palette": {
		"ink": "#100d16",
		"gold": "#ffa00d",
		"white": "#fff6e6",
		"crit": "#ff3314",
		"block": "#5aa8ff",
		"dash": "#33ccff",
		"dust": "#c7b799",
